<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mersa Gawasis</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Wadi Gawasis</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mersa Gawasis is an archaeological site on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-sea">Red Sea</a> coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>, south of Safaga, where a harbour was used by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-francia">Middle Kingdom</a> expeditions to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/land-of-punt">Punt</a> and other lands. Excavations since 2001 have found man-made caves with ship <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timber">timbers</a>, coiled ropes, cargo boxes and inscriptions naming Punt. The ships were built in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nile">Nile</a> valley, carried across the desert in pieces and reassembled on the coast.</p></div>
